# Cursor AI Rules for base_agent Project

> **📖 For detailed documentation, see [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md) and the [docs/](./docs/) directory**

## Project Overview
This is a multi-tiered AI assistant with Agentic RAG combining vector search and knowledge graph capabilities.

## Code Style & Standards
- Line length: 100 characters
- Python 3.11+ with type hints required
- Use Black formatting, Ruff linting
- MyPy for type checking
- Pre-commit hooks must pass

## Architecture Principles
- Modular design with clear separation of concerns
- Agent layer handles intelligent search capabilities
- Storage layer uses PostgreSQL/Supabase + Neo4j
- All database operations should be async
- Use dependency injection patterns

## Development Workflow
1. Always run `make format` before committing
2. Run `make check` to validate all code quality checks
3. Tests must maintain 75% coverage minimum
4. Use virtual environment (.venv)

## Common Commands
- Setup: `make setup`
- Run UI: `make run-ui`
- Run tests: `make test`
- Format code: `make format`
- Lint code: `make lint`

## Security Guidelines
- Never commit API keys or secrets
- Use parameterized SQL queries only
- Add `usedforsecurity=False` to hash functions used for non-security purposes
- Handle exceptions specifically, avoid bare except clauses

## When Making Changes
- Read CLAUDE.md for detailed architecture information
- Check existing patterns in similar modules
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Update tests for new functionality
- Document any new environment variables in .env.example

## AI Assistant Guidelines
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Always check imports and dependencies before suggesting code
- Use the existing error handling patterns
- Follow the established naming conventions
- Consider performance implications of suggestions
